              "type": "diff",
              "path": "/home/tech1savvy/cards/aws/storage/object/s3/s3.md",
              "newText": "## Features\n\n**S3 Lifecycle Management** automates object storage management through two actions\n***\n- *Transition* moves objects to cheaper storage classes over time.\n\t- Example: Standard → Standard-IA → Glacier.\n- *Expiration*: Automatically delete objects after a defined period.\n\t- Example: Delete logs after 365 days.\n\n- Encryption **At Rest** in S3:\n\t1. Server-side: data is encrypted by ==1;;AWS==.\n\t2. Client-side: data is encrypted by ==1;;you before upload==.\n\n- Encryption **In Transit** in S3: Protects data during transfer using ==SSL/TLS== protocols.\n\n**S3 Versining** allows you to keep *multiple versions* of an *object* in the *same bucket*.\n- Guards against accidental deletions or overwrites.\n- Deleting an object adds a  ==delete marker instead of removing it permanently.==\n\nWhat is Cross-Region Replication (CRR) in S3?\n***\n==Cross-Region Replication(CRR)== in S3 automatically *copies* objects to a bucket in another **AWS Region**.\n\n- Replicates:\n\t- objects\n\t- metadata\n\t- tags\n\n- Use cases:\n\t- regulatory compliance\n\t- geographic redundancy\n\t- lower latency for global users\n\t- cross-account data protection\n\n",
              "oldText": "## Features\n"
            }
          ],
          "locations": [
            {
              "path": "/home/tech1savvy/cards/aws/storage/object/s3/s3.md"
